              "name": "Transport rules",
              "fill": "$rd-fg-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Transport details belong to one leg: the one a carrier takes from the supplier, or from the forwarder when the forwarder hands off. Handoff location has no field, since it is where that leg starts. Choosing a service sets its defaults: a parcel carrier gets carrier pickup and one carrier label per carton; AGL and a freight carrier get carrier pickup and no carrier labels. Saved details show under the leg on the shipment page, as in 11.02 (Supplier / Draft packing, by way of a forwarder).",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$rd-font",
              "fontSize": 12,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
