                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "shf42",
                  "name": "Check state",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 6,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "q7op0",
                      "name": "Not checked label",
                      "fill": "$rd-fg",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Products that can share a carton aren’t checked yet",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "$rd-font",
                      "fontSize": 14,
                      "fontWeight": "500"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "M0e9U",
                      "name": "Not checked detail",
                      "fill": "$rd-fg-muted",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Amazon says which products need separate cartons when it plans the shipment. Until then, pack products Amazon handles separately, such as dangerous goods, in their own cartons.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "$rd-font",
                      "fontSize": 13,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "z6IPN",
              "name": "Implementation notes heading",
              "fill": "$rd-fg",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Design notes",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$rd-font",
              "fontSize": 16,
              "fontWeight": "600"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "L9NKi",
              "name": "Validation behavior",
              "fill": "$rd-fg-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Validate while editing and after imports. Keep drafts saved. A carton’s errors sit under its row and a product’s errors under the product, and each outlines the field it names. Rows with errors open by default; a closed row shows how many issues it has. Save draft remains available; Finish packing requires complete quantities and valid required fields. Check Amazon requirements during submission and show actionable failures without losing packing.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$rd-font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "iSEY9",
              "name": "Rules scope",
              "fill": "$rd-fg-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Use the destination marketplace, FBA packing method, product eligibility and current Amazon shipment requirements. FBA individual-unit cartons may mix compatible SKUs; case packs may not. Do not apply the 150-unit case-pack cap to all FBA individual-unit cartons. Handle single oversize-item and category-specific exceptions separately. Use Amazon’s current packing options where available.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$rd-font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "fIOnV",
              "name": "Counting rules",
              "fill": "$rd-fg-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Limits count Amazon sellable units. A six-piece retail pack sold as one listing is one sellable unit, not six. Validate SKU-to-listing mapping, quantities allocated to the shipment, positive whole counts, required measurements, duplicate carton IDs and consistent AWD templates. 50 lb is 22.6796185 kg: show and check 22.67 kg, rounded down so the limit shown is one a carton can meet.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$rd-font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "DVUO1",
              "name": "Packing groups rules",
              "fill": "$rd-fg-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "FBA cartons keep to one of Amazon’s packing groups. Amazon sets the groups only when it plans a shipment, so the packing checks use the shipment’s own groups, or the latest Amazon set for another shipment of the PO. The copy never says “packing group”, and it names products as the carton lists them: by supplier SKU, or by name for a product without one, since the supplier never sees the buyer’s SKUs. Until Amazon has planned a shipment, the Cartons section says which products can share a carton isn’t checked yet (06.18). The groups aren’t fetched live, so there’s nothing to retry.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$rd-font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "WZxnE",
              "name": "Source notes",
              "fill": "$rd-fg-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "US rules checked October 15, 2026. Standard carton examples: AWD 25 × 25 × 25 in and 50 lb; FBA 36 × 25 × 25 in and 50 lb. AWD and FBA case packs: 150 sellable units per carton. Recheck rules before implementation; product and carrier requirements can be stricter.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$rd-font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "fpvlJ",
              "name": "FBA shipping and routing source",
              "fill": "$rd-fg-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "FBA shipping and routing: https://sellercentral.amazon.com/help/hub/reference/external/200141510?locale=en-EN",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$rd-font",
              "fontSize": 12,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "CEkuK",
              "name": "FBA case-packed products source",
              "fill": "$rd-fg-muted",
