                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "f6AGQV",
                  "name": "Note",
                  "fill": "$rd-fg",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "FBA: once Amazon places the cartons, Copacker builds each Amazon shipment's pallets from the cartons sent there. Identical pallets become one entry with their count. A pallet whose cartons go to two warehouses is flagged at booking.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.4,
                  "fontFamily": "$rd-font",
                  "fontSize": 13,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "HCLcU",
                  "name": "Note",
                  "fill": "$rd-fg",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Packing list P03 lists each pallet with its cartons, size and gross weight, and each pallet label goes on the right pallet.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.4,
                  "fontFamily": "$rd-font",
                  "fontSize": 13,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "R4No7",
                  "name": "Note",
                  "fill": "$rd-fg",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "AWD: the same data maps to Amazon's PALLET packages (the cases on each pallet) once Amazon's API takes them. Until then AWD bookings send cartons only.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.4,
                  "fontFamily": "$rd-font",
                  "fontSize": 13,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "f5YqM",
                  "name": "Note",
                  "fill": "$rd-fg",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Weight is one pallet's gross weight, with the pallet itself. A closed pallet shows how many cartons and units it holds; opening it shows its cartons.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.4,
                  "fontFamily": "$rd-font",
                  "fontSize": 13,
