          "name": "Row note / Compact editor exploration",
          "fill": "#71717A",
          "content": "The adopted table design: one row per carton configuration that opens to show its products, and one row per pallet that opens to show its cartons. 06.27 is the editing spec; 06.09 B shows it inside the packing page with a pallet.",
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 16,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "OHpeD",
          "x": 40,
          "y": 9089,
          "name": "06.09 B / Supplier / Mixed-product cartons on a pallet",
          "context": "06.09 with the 06.26 carton and pallet tables (v5) in place of the carton editor cards, to judge them on the page. Packed on pallets is checked, so the Pallets section shows. Each mixed carton is its own configuration (A1, B1, C1), and all three sit on one pallet. Columns are narrowed to fit the 840px packing column. The drawstring bag is a 5-pack, so its quantities show their packs beneath. The tables have no footers; the section headers and Shipment details carry the totals, and on pallets Shipment details gives the pallets' gross weight and volume (62 kg, 0.66 m³).",
