          "id": "Pc4WG",
          "x": 1584,
          "y": 9089,
          "name": "06.27 / Packing / Carton and pallet tables, desktop",
          "context": "Exploration after 06.26 (v5). Product captions (Product, Supplier SKU, Quantity) show on a carton's first product only; later products line up on their inputs. Rows with issues open by default and complete rows stay closed; a closed row with issues shows a red count beside its units (D1–D41: 1 issue, a product needs an FNSKU); opening the row shows each issue where it is. C1 is open because the supplier opened it. The carton weight column reads Weight. No table footers: the section headers and the page's Shipment details carry the totals. Carton IDs use configuration letters. Pallet columns sit 24px apart. Pallets open and close like cartons: a closed pallet shows how many cartons and units it holds, and opening it shows its cartons. Product rows use the carton grid: Product spans Cartons to Dimensions, Supplier SKU sits under Weight, and Quantity sits under Contents. One set of column widths serves every width: Cartons 72, Count 64, Dimensions 236, Weight 104, Contents fills; pallets use Pallet 64, Dimensions 236, Weight 96, Stacking 132, 20 apart.",
