          "context": "Read-only 06.27 (v6), for a packed shipment such as 06.08. Values are text in the same columns, with no inputs, menus, add, import or remove actions, and no warnings. Rows still open to show their products (C1 is open). A pallet lists its cartons as text. Every unit is packed and every carton is on a pallet. Pallets open and close like cartons: a closed pallet shows how many cartons and units it holds, and opening it shows its cartons. Product rows use the carton grid: Product spans Cartons to Dimensions, Supplier SKU sits under Weight, and Quantity sits under Contents. One set of column widths serves every width: Cartons 72, Count 64, Dimensions 236, Weight 104, Contents fills; pallets use Pallet 64, Dimensions 236, Weight 96, Stacking 132, 20 apart. Count is left-aligned here so it doesn't run into Dimensions.",
