        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "KC4a2",
          "x": 40,
          "y": 10500,
          "name": "Row heading / Carrier labels matched by weight and size",
          "fill": "#18181B",
          "content": "Carrier labels matched by weight and size",
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 24,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "x3LW9w",
          "x": 40,
          "y": 10536,
          "name": "Row note / Carrier labels matched by weight and size",
          "fill": "#71717A",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 2320,
          "content": "Dropped PDFs are split into labels that wait in Not placed. A label whose printed weight and size fit only one carton configuration, within a pound and an inch, goes onto that configuration’s cartons by itself. Fill cartons in order places the rest, or drag each onto its carton. A label goes on a carton only once it has a tracking number.",
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 16,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "AzpHf",
          "x": 40,
          "y": 10600,
          "name": "Board title / 10.11",
          "fill": "$rd-fg",
          "content": "10.11 / Buyer / Upload carrier labels, labels not placed",
          "fontFamily": "$rd-font",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "QsIzH",
          "x": 40,
          "y": 10626,
          "name": "10.11 / Buyer / Upload carrier labels, labels not placed",
          "context": "A shipment of 36 cartons: A1 to A24 and B1 to B12. The buyer dropped the 3 PDFs their carrier gave them on Not placed, which is where PDFs go: dropping one anywhere on it, or browsing, splits it into labels there. A PDF dropped again adds none of the labels already here. Labels wait in Not placed until they go on a carton. None printed a weight and size that fits only one carton configuration, so nothing was placed by itself (10.12 shows that case). Each label shows its tracking number, read from its text or, when the PDF is a picture as UPS labels bought in Shopify are, from its barcode. Below it is the weight and size it prints, or else its file and page. Page 6’s number couldn’t be read: it says No tracking number, its grip is dimmed because it can’t go on a carton yet, and Add opens its preview at the Tracking number field (10.13 states). Fill cartons in order puts every waiting label that has a number on the empty cartons in file and page order. A label is dragged onto a carton, and its thumbnail opens the preview (10.13), whose Carton field places it without dragging. Each empty carton’s ID is pressed into its drop zone. Save is off until a carton has a label. Beside the board: Not placed before any PDF, and with a PDF dragged over it.",
          "clip": true,
          "width": 1040,
          "fill": "$rd-muted",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "padding": 16,
