        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "h7Kapz",
          "x": 1160,
          "y": 10626,
          "name": "10.12 / Buyer / Upload carrier labels, placed by weight and size",
          "context": "The same 36 cartons. The buyer dropped fedex-a.pdf, 24 FedEx labels that print their weight and size (27.3 lb, 24 × 16 × 16 in). Within a pound and an inch only A1 to A24 fit, so the 24 went onto those cartons by themselves, in page order. ups-b.pdf’s 12 UPS labels are pictures: their numbers come from their barcodes, and their weight and size only once a preview reads their text, so they wait in Not placed. The buyer put pages 1 and 2 on B1 and B2 and is dragging page 3 onto B3, which says where it will go. A placed label shows the weight and size it prints, or else its file and page, and its X sends it back to Not placed.",
